:: Days of the week in Irish [days regular] {"position":"1350,375","size":"100,100"}
<h1>The Days of the Week in Irish</h1>
<p>On the following pages you will hear various speakers reciting days of the week. You are invited to copy them and record the days of the week in your own voice.</p>

<p>These recordings come from the Tionscadal Gréasáin Cheirníní Doegen, The Doegen Records Web Project, wich is an archive of Irish dialect sound recordings made during 1928-31. It contains folktales, songs and other material recited by native Irish speakers from 17 counties. Crucially, it includes examples of dialects that are now extinct.</p>

<p>In 1926 the Irish government asked Dr Doegen to make recordings of Irish speech in the Gaeltacht and in areas of the country where Irish had suffered decline. The Department of Education asked the Royal Irish Academy if it would organize such a scheme (Survey of Dialects) and the Academy’s Irish Studies Committee undertook the task. The recordings were made by Dr Doegen and his assistant Karl Tempel between 1928 and 1931.</p>

<p>The collection includes a number of recordings of days of the week which we have broken out into samples for each weekday.</p>

[[Monday]] [[Tuesday]] [[Wednesday]] [[Thursday]] [[Friday]] [[Saturday]] [[Sunday]]

<p>The Speakers and Dialects are listed below, along with the citations for the digital objects from which these clips were taken.</p>

''Tomás Ó Gallchobhair from Co. Donegal''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. Laethanta na seachtaine.The days of the week. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1931-10-03). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.r7829447m" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.r7829447m</a></p>

''Domhnall Ó Céilleachair from Co. Cork''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. An feirmeoir agus an bacach; laethanta na seachtaine; focail.The farmer and the beggar; days of the week; words. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1928-09-03). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.pn89sw062" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.pn89sw062</a></p>

''Seán Mag Uidhir from Co. Cavan''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. Laethanta na seachtaine.The days of the week. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1931-09-23). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.9w03fr48g" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.9w03fr48g</a></p>

''Áine Ní Mhuireadhaigh from Co. Donegal''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. Laethanta na seachtaine.The days of the week. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1931-09-30). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.8g851874c" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.8g851874c</a></p>

''Eoin Ó Cianáin from Co. Tyrone''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. Laethanta na seachtaine.The days of the week. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1931-09-24). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.54260016c" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.54260016c</a></p>

''Brighid Ní Chaslaigh from Co. Louth''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. Laethanta na seachtaine.The days of the week. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1931-09-25). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.2z119c690" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.2z119c690</a></p>

<p>The background image on each of these pages is An Post Museum and Archive &#91;Depositor&#93;. Mounted postmen - allowance for animal feed. Department of Posts & Telegraphs. (1926). Image &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2024) &#91;Publisher&#93. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.j960fw194" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.j960fw194</a></p>




