:: counting [counting regular] {"position":"525,525","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Counting in Irish</h1>

<p>On this page you will hear a recitation of numbers by Mícheál Turraoin from Co. Waterford. It was recorded primarily for phonetic purposes. It is one of 30 such items in the Doegen collection. You are invited to copy it and record yourself counting from one to ten in Irish, in your own voice.</p>

<p>This recording comes from the Tionscadal Gréasáin Cheirníní Doegen, The Doegen Records Web Project, wich is an archive of Irish dialect sound recordings made during 1928-31. It contains folktales, songs and other material recited by native Irish speakers from 17 counties. Crucially, it includes examples of dialects that are now extinct.</p>

<p>In 1926 the Irish government asked Dr Doegen to make recordings of Irish speech in the Gaeltacht and in areas of the country where Irish had suffered decline. The Department of Education asked the Royal Irish Academy if it would organize such a scheme (Survey of Dialects) and the Academy’s Irish Studies Committee undertook the task. The recordings were made by Dr Doegen and his assistant Karl Tempel between 1928 and 1931.</p>

''Source:''
<p>Royal Irish Academy &#91;Depositor&#93;. Uimhreacha.Numbers. Dr Wilhelm Doegen. (1928-09-05). Sound &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2022) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.ww72r097k" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.ww72r097k</a></p>

<audio id="audioClip" preload="auto" controls>
<source src="https://digital-repository-of-ireland.github.io/SpeakLikeMe/assets/numbers.mp3">
</audio>

[[Let me try!|record1to10]]

<p>The background image on this page is The Discovery Programme &#91;Depositor&#93;. Plan orthoimage of a point cloud of Martello tower no. 9 (SMR No.: DU023-029009-), Dalkey Island, County Dublin. The terrestrial laser scanning data was captured on 04/04/2022.. The Discovery Programme, CHERISH Project. (04/04/2022). Image &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2025) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.ww72rd220" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.ww72rd220</a></p>



:: digipresterms [teármaíocht regular] {"position":"775,725","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Digital Preservation Terms</h1>

<p>On the following pages you will hear a variety of useful Digital Preservation Terms from the Taifeadtaí de Théarmaíocht an Bhuanchoimeádta Dhigitigh collection. You are invited to copy them and record these terms in your own voice.</p>

<p>This work builds on a project by the DRI and Dublin City University to create a standardised set of Irish language terms relating to digital preservation. The list was published in May 2025 as the "Téarmaíocht an Bhuanchoimeádta Dhigitigh:  Gluais Ghaeilge do thaisclanna agus do chartlannaithe", or  "Digital Preservation Terminology: An Irish language glossary for repositories and archivists".</p>

<p>In 2026, reference recordings of the terms were made by Niamh Ní Charra, forming the <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.1831ss39z">Taifeadtaí de Théarmaíocht an Bhuanchoimeádta Dhigitigh collection</a>. A selection of these recordings are listed below.</p>

[[Digital Preservation]]
[[Born-Digital Record]]
[[Community Archive]]
[[Descriptive Metadata]]
[[Long-term Preservation]]
[[Persistent Identifier]]
[[Reuse Licence]]
[[Web Archiving]]

''Source:''
<p>Digital Repository of Ireland &#91;Depositor&#93;. Taifeadtaí de Théarmaíocht an Bhuanchoimeádta Dhigitigh.Digital Preservation Terminology Recordings. Niamh Ní Charra, archivist, University of Galway. (2025-05-25). Collection &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2026) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.1831ss39z" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.1831ss39z</a></p>

<p>The background image on each of these pages is National Botanic Gardens &#91;Depositor&#93;. Papaver rhoeas L.. DBN herbarium. (1943). Image &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2025) &#91;Publisher&#93;. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.x346t635v" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.x346t635v</a></p>


:: placenames [placenames regular] {"position":"1250,925","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Irish Placenames</h1>

<p>On the following pages you will hear audio recordings from the Logainm Sound Recordings (LSR) collection. This is an archival copy of the sound recordings carried out under the Dublin City University Logainm Placenames Database of Ireland research project (Logainm). Dr Brian Ó Raghallaigh is the Principal Investigator on the Logainm project and supervised the sound recording project. LSR was created by Dr Brian Ó Raghallaigh (DCU) and Dr Patrick Egan (MTU) for the purposes of preservation and reuse.</p>

<p>Sound recordings include names of baronies, civil parishes, electoral divisions, centres of population and major natural features (such as rivers, lakes, mountains), as well as townlands in Gaeltacht areas (Irish-language form only) and the main streets of Dublin.</p>

<p>For each county a single speaker was chosen, one who was raised in the county and who was familiar with its placenames. Native Irish speakers were chosen in counties containing a Gaeltacht region. English speakers with fluent Irish and knowledge of the pronunciation of the English forms of the placenames were chosen in the other counties.</p>

<p>These recordings have been selected from the Antrim Subcollection of the Logainm Sound Recordings, and include well-known places close to Belfast.</p>


[[Belfast - Béal Feirste|Belfast]]
[[Antrim - Aontroim|Antrim]]
[[Larne - Latharnah|Larne]]
[[Lisburn - Lios na gCearrbhach|Lisburn]]
[[Ballycastle - Baile an Chaistil|Ballycastle]]
[[Bushmills - Muileann na Buaise|Bushmills]]
[[Carrickfergus - Carraig Fhearghais|Carrickfergus]]
[[Ballymena - An Baile Meánach|Ballymena]]
[[Portrush - Port Rois|Portrush]]
[[Giant's Causeway - Clochán an Aifir|GiantsCauseway]]

''Source:''
<p>Logainm Sound Recordings.Taifeadtaí Fuaime Logainm. Brian Ó Raghallaigh, Patrick Egan. (2007–2021). Collection &#91;Type&#93. Digital Repository of Ireland (2024) &#91;Publisher&#93. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.jd47gr915" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.jd47gr915</a></p>
</p>

<p>The background image on each of these pages is Technological University of the Shannon &#91;Depositor&#93;. Map of location and approximate extent of Pat O'Carroll site on Shannon. Shannon Free Airport Development Company. . Image &#91;Type&#93;. Digital Repository of Ireland (2025) &#91;Publisher&#93. <a href="https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.n584bw60x" target="_blank">https://doi.org/10.7486/DRI.n584bw60x</a></p>


